      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of \"letting go\" isn't about magically erasing the debt; it's about stopping the fight against the inevitable. Those expectations and failures are just noise, and you don't have to listen to them anymore. Real relief comes when you stop trying to force a way out and instead just allow the pressure to dissipate, one small, quiet moment at a time. You don't have to fix the whole mess; you just have to stop trying to carry it all.",
      "source": "target",
